                        "entry_id": "9d39dde5-138d-34fb-aa38-d98d827b5da7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Abbreviation of reactive oxygen species."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ba846f3-d431-462f-aaaf-7643042d4ca3",
                                "sense_id": "8108ec6e-611e-3385-a608-bcb2ff3cae23",
                                "text": "O₂^(•−) and OH^• are highly unstable (half-life at the level of microseconds and nanoseconds, respectively) and cannot cross membrane, while H₂O₂, though not a free radical but a ROS, is relatively stable (half-life around 1 ms) (Møller et al. 2007) and can cross membranes through aquaporins."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3252a1f9-ac08-4b58-b5ff-c759e0dbfc29",
                                "sense_id": "8108ec6e-611e-3385-a608-bcb2ff3cae23",
                                "text": "Either way, a set of antioxidants worked to reduce the levels of ROS, and the [fruit] flies could live to the ripe old age of 40 days… if not a teensy bit longer! But most importantly, this demonstrated that the death from lack of sleep was not only correlated with the production of ROS, but caused by it."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
